      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I just tested the patch and it doesn't fix the issue. It does make the responseDate correct, but it then shifts the record dates so they're wrong.</p>\n\n<p>The date parsing in OAIResponder is hopelessly broken. A proper fix should probably employ the DateUtility class to do all the date parsing/UTC-ifying, as is done with the rest of the server code.</p>",
     "created": "10/May/11 10:40 PM",
     "id": "11951",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10704/comment/11951",
     "updateAuthor": {
